FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied (meant for upstream):
- Add `src/fortify.rs` implementing `__chk_fail` and the `__*_chk` bounds-checking entry points for string/memory (`__memcpy_chk`, `__memmove_chk`, `__memset_chk`, `__strcpy_chk`, `__stpcpy_chk`, `__strncpy_chk`, `__stpncpy_chk`, `__strcat_chk`, `__strncat_chk`), stdio (`__vsnprintf_chk`, `__snprintf_chk`, `__vsprintf_chk`, `__sprintf_chk`, `__fgets_chk`), and unistd (`__read_chk`, `__pread_chk`, `__readlink_chk`, `__readlinkat_chk`, `__getcwd_chk`).
- Add `_FORTIFY_SOURCE` (levels 1, 2, and 3 when `__builtin_dynamic_object_size` is available) detection in `include/features.h` and fortified inline wrappers in `include/bits/fortify-{string,stdio,unistd}.h`, included from `<string.h>`, `<stdio.h>`, and `<unistd.h>` when optimizing with `_FORTIFY_SOURCE > 0`.

